								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12016#msg12016"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12016#msg12016">Re: new car, dealerships mark up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> October 26, 2004, 10:19:00 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I personally think that you are right. Because it is so new (and wicked cool by the way) the demand is high, and the dealers arent going to have to haggle as much. Next year might be easer to haggle. I guess it boils down to, is 5K worth you having the car right now. That is personal choice.<br /><br />Gotta say, that that is the first Ford product I have ever seriously considered owning. That thing rocks.
						</td>
