								Posts: 47<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://forums.gucomics.com/images/avatars/20002703583fbef1af3a4d3.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=265105278" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=265105278&amp;img=5" alt="265105278" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/Wyztyz" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="Wyztyz" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=Wyztyz"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=Wyztyz&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="Wyztyz" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=Wyztyz&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="Wyztyz" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=167"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.dragonsfist.org" title="Dragons Fist" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:wyztyz@aol.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12806#msg12806"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12806#msg12806">Re: new car, dealerships mark up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #10 on:</b> November 24, 2004, 01:24:17 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I happen to be a Finance Director at an auto mall in Southern California.  I&#039;m the person behind the scenes getting loans approved with the lender for auto dealership customers.  Customers almost never get to meet me.  <br /><br />The new 2005 Mustang GT is in high demand.  Our Ford Dealership cannot keep up with the supply and demand of this vehicle atm.  The Markup is due to the high demand on the vehicle since its a new body style.  The demand can&#039;t keep up with production.  Other vehicles like the Ford Explorer are being sold under invoice (under cost).  It&#039;s just the market dictating the price atm.  If you are patient, wait until the newness of the vehicle has worn off.  <br /><br />Fleet managers are salesman too btw.  They do get paid commission usually its a higher commission that normal sales people since they don&#039;t get a chance to deal with the public often.  They generally deal in quantity sales, government sales or internet sales but the public is always welcome to deal with them.  With the fleet department there is not much haggling.  There is a set amount over invoice for every car.  <br /><br />Many times if you are a good haggler, you get a better deal through the normal sales department.  Through the normal sales department try to deal directly with the Sales Manager instead of the Sales Person so there is less back and forth haggling.  Let the sales person test drive you in the car you want then Ask to directly speak with the Sales Manager.  Ask to see the invoice before you make an offer on a vehicle.  If its a reasonable offer over invoice, any dealer will take it depending on the demand for the vehicle.   Try to go the last few days of the month to buy a vehicle.  They have to get rid of any inventory before they pay any &quot;Flooring&quot; on the car.  Flooring is the interest charged to inventory each vehicle every month.  Flooring costs the dealership hundred of dollars for each vehicle still in inventory at the end of every month so they are interested in moving the vehicle especially if the unit has been there more than 30 days.  <br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: November 24, 2004, 01:40:37 pm by Wyztyz</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Wyztyz Wyckedwytz<br />Wizardess of the Solusek Ro and the 66th Season<br />Broodmother and Guild Leader to Dragons Fist on Rodcet Nife<br />RL &gt; EQ.  Keep it in perspective!
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
