						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=57" title="View the profile of Givins">Givins</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 144<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://mark.scns.com/eq/givins.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Illuminating mobs since 2001<br />
								<br />
								<a href="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/about_me/1,,,00.html?Uin=5226347" target="_blank"><img src="http://web.icq.com/whitepages/online?icq=5226347&amp;img=5" alt="5226347" width="18" height="18" border="0" /></a>
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=57"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:ktadema@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12818#msg12818"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1208.msg12818#msg12818">Re: new car, dealerships mark up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> November 24, 2004, 09:02:22 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Wow, good post Wyztyz.&nbsp; I&#039;ve heard that the last of the month on the last month of the year (December) is actually the optimal time, since they also have to deal with end of the year inventory and taxes.&nbsp; I&#039;ve also heard, and this makes sense to me, that it&#039;s best to shop late in the day.&nbsp; That way, they are less inclined to play negotiating games with you, since they want to get off on time.&nbsp; <br /><br />Something I did when I was shopping for a new car back in 99 was to get what I thought was a good low price from one dealer.&nbsp; Then I would call another dealer and tell them that I have an offer to buy a car for X price.&nbsp; I had to make a decision in the next hour (a lie, but I wanted them to hurry up).&nbsp; Can they beat it?&nbsp; At first, they would say yes.&nbsp; I called yet another dealership and said I had yet another low price and ask if they could beat it.&nbsp; I played that game with about 5-6 dealerships until they started saying that there was no way they could beat that price.&nbsp; That was when I knew I was at least in the right ballpark.&nbsp; <br /><br />But looking for tips on that new Mustang is probably going to be moot.&nbsp; Everyone has been gushing about it.&nbsp; I&#039;m pretty sure that for once, Ford will be able to ask whatever price they want until the customers that are crazy enough to pay stupid prices on it have all got their cars.&nbsp; I&#039;m sure the best advice, though you won&#039;t like it, is to wait on the demand to go down on those cars.&nbsp; That will take a while, months, maybe even a year.&nbsp; <br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
